Error fixtures for the embedded Ohm grammar. Each member has flag `o`,
so the archive needs no grammar member and no docker. Each .error member
is the output of `ohm-cli test match_error` on the .txt member of the
same test. Flag `N` removes the trailing newline of the .txt member, so
the input is as in error-reporting prd section 3.
-- star_x.txt --
G {
  S = *x
}
-- star_x.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 7:
  1 | G {
> 2 |   S = *x
            ^
  3 | }
-- star_x.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 7: match failed
-- unclosed.txt --
G {
  S = "a"
-- unclosed.o.error --
Line 3, col 1:
  2 |   S = "a"
> 3 | 
      ^
-- unclosed.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 10:
  1 | G {
> 2 |   S = "a"
               ^
-- unclosed.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 10: match failed
-- trailing_h.txt --
G { S = "a" }
H
-- trailing_h.o.N.error --
Line 2, col 2:
  1 | G { S = "a" }
> 2 | H
       ^
-- trailing_h.o.N.s.error --
Line 2, col 2: match failed
